// final class — cannot be extended
public final class String {  // can't do: class MyString extends String
    // ...
}

// final method — cannot be overridden
public class Base {
    public final void initialize() {
        // critical initialization — no subclass can change this
    }
    public void otherMethod() { }  // subclasses can override this
}

public class Derived extends Base {
    // @Override
    // void initialize() { }  // COMPILE ERROR — final method
    @Override
    void otherMethod() { }  // fine
}
```

Well-known final classes: `String`, `Integer`, `Long`, `Double`, `Math`, `System`
